{
  "id": "glycerine___boiling_and_freezing_points",
  "title": "Glycerine - Boiling and Freezing Points",
  "description": "Calculator for boiling and freezing points of glycerine (glycerin/glycerol) aqueous solutions. The boiling points decrease with increased glycerine concentration, while freezing points decrease until 66.7% glycerine concentration, then increase above that threshold.",
  "type": "calculator",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Glycerine Solution Properties\n\nThis calculator determines the boiling and freezing points of glycerine-water mixtures based on concentration.\n\n### Key Facts:\n- **Boiling points** decrease with increased glycerine concentration\n- **Freezing points** decrease until glycerine concentration reaches 66.7% (mass)\n- Above 66.7% glycerine, freezing points begin to increase\n- All data measured at 60°F (15.6°C) reference temperature for specific gravity"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "glycerine_concentration",
          "label": "Glycerine Concentration",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "% by mass",
          "defaultValue": 70
        },
        {
          "id": "temperature_unit",
          "label": "Temperature Unit",
          "type": "select",
          "defaultValue": "celsius",
          "options": [
            {
              "label": "Celsius (°C)",
              "value": "celsius"
            },
            {
              "label": "Fahrenheit (°F)",
              "value": "fahrenheit"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "freezing_point_celsius",
          "label": "Freezing Point",
          "unit": "°C",
          "formula": "IF(inputs.glycerine_concentration >= 66.7, -46.1 + (inputs.glycerine_concentration - 66.7) * 0.5, -51 + (66.7 - inputs.glycerine_concentration) * 0.3)"
        },
        {
          "id": "boiling_point_celsius",
          "label": "Boiling Point",
          "unit": "°C",
          "formula": "100 - (inputs.glycerine_concentration * 0.5)"
        },
        {
          "id": "specific_gravity",
          "label": "Specific Gravity (at 60°F)",
          "unit": "g/cm³",
          "formula": "1.0 + (inputs.glycerine_concentration * 0.0026)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Glycerine Concentration (% mass)",
        "Specific Gravity (60°F)",
        "Freezing Point (°C)",
        "Boiling Point (°C)"
      ],
